ENTRY            D1097   20260609   20261124   20261124       D153
SUBENT        D1097001   20260609   20261124   20261124       D153
BIB                 12         46
TITLE      Deuteron-induced charged-particle emission on
            molybdenum at low energies
AUTHOR     (E.Simeckova, M.Avrigeanu, J.Mrazek, X.Ledoux,
            J.Novak, M.Stefanik, M.Ansorge, A.Cassisa, J.Kozic,
            C.Costache, V.Avrigeanu)
INSTITUTE  (3CZRUJF,3RUMBUC,2FR GAN)
REFERENCE  (J,PR/C,113,044604,2026)
           #doi:10.1103/1yw3-6mmp
REL-REF    (O,D1072001,E.Simeckova+,J,PR/C,111,044612,2025)
            Measured Tc isotope activation cross sections for
            d+natMo
FACILITY   (CYCLO,3CZRUJF) U120-M cyclotron
           (LINAC,2FR GAN) GANIL/SPIRAL2 linear accelerator
SAMPLE     All Mo and Al foils (15 mm diameter, 99.9% purity) and
            weighed to determine the exact thickness.
DETECTOR   (HPGE)
METHOD     (BCINT) Beam flux determined by Faraday cup
           (STTA)
           . 1) NPI CAS setup:
            Mo foils were interleaved with Al foils as
             additional beam current monitor and as an energy
             degrader.
           . 2) GANIL stacked foil 1 setup:
            Mo foils (25 um for 30 MeV) interleaved with
            Al foils (50 um)
           . 3) GANIL stacked foil 2 setup:
             Mo foils (50 um) interleaved with Al foils (50 um)
           (SITA)
           . 4) GANIL single foil setup:
             Mo foils (50 um above 30 MeV and 25 um below 30 MeV)
           (ACTIV,GSPEC)
           . 1) NPI CAS setup:
            Measurement repeated during 100 days.
           . 2,3) GANIL stacked foil 1 and 2 setup:
            Irradiated for 10 min. Cooled for ~4 h and measured
             for 10 days.
           . 4) GANIL single foil setup:
             Irradiated for 4 min. Cooled for ~50 sec and
             measured for typically 20 min
ERR-ANALYS (ERR-T) Total uncertainty are propagated from:
           . Statistical uncertainty in determining peak area
           (ERR-1) HPGE efficiency (2%)
           (ERR-2) Beam current (5%)
           (ERR-3) Foil thickness (2%)
STATUS     (APRVD) Proof-read by E.Simeckova (2026-06-23)
HISTORY    (20260609C) VT
ENDBIB              46
COMMON               3          3
ERR-1      ERR-2      ERR-3
PER-CENT   PER-CENT   PER-CENT
         2.         5.         2.
ENDCOMMON            3
ENDSUBENT           53
SUBENT        D1097002   20260609   20261124   20261124       D153
